  "title": "Serpent Mound (Great Serpent Mound)",
  "summary": "Serpent Mound is a 411-metre (1,348-foot) earthen serpent effigy, 1.2 to 1.5 metres high, overlooking Ohio Brush Creek in Adams County, Ohio. Long attributed to the Adena, charcoal samples dated to about A.D. 1070 pointed to the Fort Ancient culture, while a 2014 study gave 381 to 44 B.C. Its builders and date remain contested.",
